{"t": 1788690696.089247, "step": 3, "turn": 10, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.82, margin 0.46)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.64)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (5 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788690799.4667468, "step": 4, "turn": 11, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_4", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_4", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.62)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.68)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.82, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.56)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (4 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state. Let me parse through all the details.\n\nOccupied cells: There are several items listed with their positions, feed values, and whether they're feedable or spawnable. Empty cells are (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1). The mana bar is at 100% full, which means collecting isn't a good idea because the bar is already maxed. Satiety is 508/2000, so there's still room to feed.\n\nThe active cravings are for an Eye Monster. The board has a peasant (champion) at (3,2), which is a champion. The Peasant is a champion, so attacking it would be possible if there's a creature with damage value.\n\nLooking at the Feats: There's a \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice\" feat that's 0/0 completed. Since the peasant is on the board, attacking it might be part of this feat. The other feats are about merging and building a Supply Cupboard, which is already done.\n\nThe Best spawn hint is supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3) -> eyeball, but there's also grave_lvl3 at (4,3). However, the user mentioned that the best spawn is supplycupboard_lvl1. But wait, the board has a Supply Cupboard level 1 at (1,3), which can spawn eyeballs. But the current state shows that the Supply Cupboard is already built (since it's listed as \"done\" in the Feats). Wait, the Feats line says \"Build a Supply Cupboard. (done)\", so maybe the Supply Cupboard is already constructed.\n\nWait, the board has supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3), which is a spawn station. But since the feat to build it is done, perhaps it's already built. However, the user might have multiple stations. The key here is that the Supply Cupboard is a spawn station, but the current state shows it's level 1.\n\nBut looking at the board, there are empty cells (4 of 20), so spawning would be possible. However, the mana bar is full, so spawning the grave might not be possible because grave requires Mana. Wait, the mana bar is 100% full,"}
{"t": 1788690834.856236, "step": 4, "turn": 12, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_4", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_4", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.62)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.68)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.82, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.56)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (4 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state with all the occupied cells and their details. Let me go through each part step by step.\n\nFirst, the empty cells are (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1). There are four empty cells. The board is 5x4, so 20 total cells. Four empty means it's not too congested, but there's room for spawns or merges.\n\nLooking at the occupied cells:\n\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2: feed 5, FEEDABLE\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1: feed 2, FEEDABLE\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1: feed 60, dmg 25\n- (0,3) necromerger: UNKNOWN, don't feed\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1: feed 2, FEEDABLE\n- (1,2) cauldron: UNKNOWN, don't feed\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1: SPAWNABLE\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2: feed 5, FEEDABLE\n- (2,1) bone: feed 1, FEEDABLE\n- (2,2) ribcage: feed 2, FEEDABLE\n- (2,3) eyeball: feed 1, FEEDABLE\n- (3,2) peasant: champion, feed 1\n- (3,3) eyeinajar: feed 2, FEEDABLE\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5: score 1.00, margin 0.55\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1: SPAWNABLE\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3: SPAWNABLE\n\nThe best spawn hint is supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3), which spawns eyeball and costs Slime. But the user has a mana bar at ~100% full, so maybe not the best time to spawn? Wait, but the mana bar is full, so spawning might not be ideal because it uses Slime. However, the supplycupboard_lvl1 is a spawn station that can be used to get eyeballs, which are feedable.\n\nWait, the user's satiety is 5"}
{"t": 1788690844.933696, "step": 4, "turn": 13, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.62)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.68)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.82, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.56)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (4 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788690920.247173, "step": 5, "turn": 14, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_5", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_5", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.62)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.60)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.82, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.56)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (3 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: board_management (board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down. The user provided the current board state after a get_board_state call. My job is to figure out the best move based on the rules and the given data.\n\nFirst, looking at the occupied cells. There are several items here. Let me check for possible merges. The \"Best merge\" hint says eyeball (2,3) + (3,1). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE], so they can be merged. But wait, the merge chain for eyeball is to summon an Eye Monster. The craving is for an Eye Monster, which is a level 5. So merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster, which is exactly what the craving needs. However, the current state shows that there are two eyeballs: one at (2,3) and another at (3,1). \n\nWait, but the Feats line mentions \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat. Since the user has a craving for an Eye Monster, merging these two would fulfill part of the craving. But the problem is, the current state shows that the craving is still ongoing (0/2), so each feed of the craved item counts toward the quota. However, merging the eyeballs would create the Eye Monster, which is the craved item. Wait, but the Eye Monster is a different item than the eyeball. Let me check the item descriptions.\n\nLooking at the item list: \"eyeinajar\" (feed 2) and \"eyeball\" (feed 1). The Eye Monster is probably the next level. The merge chain for the Eye Monster isn't explicitly listed, but the Feats mention \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster.\" So maybe merging two eyeballs creates an Eye Monster. But according to the item list, the supplycupboard levels spawn eyeinajar, which is a lower level. Hmm.\n\nWait, the user's board has (3,2) as peasant (champion), which is a different type. The craving is for eyemonster, so maybe the Eye Monster is the craved item. But how does merging eyeballs lead to that? Maybe the merge chain is eyeball -> eyeinajar -> Eye Monster. But the current state shows two eyeballs. If you merge two eyeballs, do they become an eyeinajar or something else?\n\nWait, looking at the item list: \"supplycupboard_lvl1\" spawns eyeinajar. So maybe the Eye Monster is a higher"}
{"t": 1788690955.814016, "step": 5, "turn": 15, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_5", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_5", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.62)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.60)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.82, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.56)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (3 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: board_management (board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's see. The user provided the current board state and wants me to decide the best move. Let me go through the details.\n\nFirst, looking at the board state:\n\n- There are empty cells: (1,0), (3,0), (4,1). So the board isn't too full.\n- The \"Best merge\" hint is eyeball (2,3) + (3,1). Both are [FEEDABLE], so merging them is valid.\n- The Feats line mentions \"Build a Supply Cupboard. (done)\", which means that's already completed. So maybe the next step is to focus on other feats or manage the board.\n\nWait, the suggested direction is board_management because the board is congested. But there are empty cells, so maybe merging isn't the priority here. However, the Best merge hint is present, so it's a valid move.\n\nAlso, the user mentioned that if there are multiple tools to call, they can be called in one round. But in this case, the task is to output only the action, not tool calls. Wait, no\u2014the user says \"never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action.\" So I need to choose between merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle.\n\nThe Best merge hint is eyeball (2,3) and (3,1). Both are FEEDABLE, so merging them would be valid. Let me check if there's any reason not to merge. The Feats line has \"Merge things 250 times\" which is a merge feat, but since it's 0/0, maybe the priority is on the Best merge hint.\n\nAlso, the board has empty cells, so spawning might be an option. But the Best spawn hint isn't listed here; the user says \"Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1\". However, the Supply Cupboard is already built (since the feat is done), so maybe spawning from it isn't necessary. The grave levels are present, but the Best merge is more urgent.\n\nWait, the user's board state shows that there's a \"Best merge\" hint, which is a priority. So merging those two eyeballs would be the best move. Let me check if they can be merged. Both are eyeball (feed 1), so merging two of the same should create a higher level. The merge chain for eyeball isn't"}
{"t": 1788690966.4147708, "step": 5, "turn": 16, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.62)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.60)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.82, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.56)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (3 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: board_management (board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [2, 3], \"b\": [3, 1]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [2, 3], \"b\": [3, 1]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788691067.525687, "step": 6, "turn": 17, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_6", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_6", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.80, margin 0.44)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down step by step. The user provided the current board state, and I need to figure out the best move based on the rules and the given information.\n\nFirst, looking at the occupied cells:\n\n- There are two eyeinajar (3,1) and (3,3). The Best merge hint says to merge these two. Eyeinajar is part of the Eye Monster chain. Merging them would create a higher level Eye Monster, which might be useful for the craving or future merges.\n\nNext, check if there's a craving. The board state mentions \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So the player needs to fulfill this craving. But wait, the current cells are eyeinajar, which is a lower level. To get the Eye Monster, you need to merge two eyeinajar into one. Wait, but the chain might be different. Let me check the item descriptions.\n\nFrom the item list: \"eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\". The description says \"Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\" So merging two eyeinajar would create an Eye Monster. But the current state shows two eyeinajar on the board. However, the Best merge hint is for merging those two.\n\nWait, but the Feats line says: \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]\". So the player hasn't reached that level yet. But the current cells are eyeinajar, which is probably level 1 or 2. Wait, the item list shows \"eyeinajar\" as feed value 2. Maybe it's a lower level.\n\nBut the Best merge hint is for merging (3,1) and (3,3), both eyeinajar. So merging them would create an Eye Monster. But the craving is for eyemonster, which might be the next step. However, the player needs to check if there's a better move.\n\nAlso, looking at the empty cells: (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1). There are four empty cells. The board is not too congested. But the Feats line mentions \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" which is 0/0 completed. The peasant is a champion on the board at (3,2). So maybe attacking the peasant would be a good move.\n\nWait, the player has a peasant (champion) at (3,2). The item description for peasant says"}
{"t": 1788691102.915314, "step": 6, "turn": 18, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_6", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_6", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.80, margin 0.44)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's see. The user provided the current board state and wants me to decide the best move. Let me go through the details carefully.\n\nFirst, looking at the occupied cells. There are several items here. The key points from the board state:\n\n- Empty cells: (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1) \u2014 four empty spots.\n- Best merge hint is eyeinajar (3,1) and (3,3). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE] with feed values of 2 each. Merging them would create an Eye Monster, which is the current craving. The craving is for an Eye Monster, so merging these two should fulfill part of the craving.\n\nWait, the craving is \"eyemonster\" and the merge of two eyeinajar (which are level 1) would make a higher level? Wait, according to the item chain, supplycupboard_lvl1 spawns eyeinajar. But the Eye Monster is probably a different item. Let me check the item list.\n\nLooking at the items: there's an \"eyeinajar\" which is a feedable item with feed value 2. The merge chain for eyeinajar isn't explicitly listed here, but maybe it's part of summoning an Eye Monster. Wait, the user mentioned in the past learnings that \"supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\" and higher levels spawn eyeinajar. But the craving is for an Eye Monster, which might be a different item.\n\nWait, the board state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So the current craving is to get an Eye Monster. The Eye Monster isn't listed in the occupied cells. So maybe merging two eyeinajar would create an Eye Monster? Let me check the item descriptions.\n\nIn the items learned: \"eyeinajar\" has a description that says \"Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\" Wait, no\u2014the popup for eyeinajar says \"Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\" Hmm, maybe there's a typo. Wait, looking at the provided item data:\n\n- Item eyeinajar (popup): \"Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\" Wait, no, the user's item list shows:\n\n\"## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\"\n\nWait, but in the provided data, it says \"eyeinajar\" is for merging into an Eye Monster"}
{"t": 1788691113.127722, "step": 6, "turn": 19, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.80, margin 0.44)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [3, 1], \"b\": [3, 3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [3, 1], \"b\": [3, 3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788691222.508481, "step": 7, "turn": 20, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_7", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_7", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: [(3, 3)]\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (6 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "proactive_identify_1788691187075", "function": {"name": "identify_item", "arguments": "{\"cells\": [[3, 3]]}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "proactive_identify_1788691187075", "content": "{\"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"eyemonster_lvl1\", \"cell\": [3, 3], \"merge_info\": \"two Eye Monster -> Eye Monster of the next level\", \"description\": \"Merge to summon a higher lvl Eye Monster.\"}]}"}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's see. The user provided the current board state and the tool responses. I need to figure out the best move based on the given information.\n\nFirst, looking at the board state:\n\n- There are several items listed. The key points here are:\n  - Empty cells: (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\n  - Unidentified cell at (3,3) which was identified as eyemonster_lvl1.\n  - Mana is ~100% full, so collecting isn't a good idea here.\n  - Satiety is 508/2000 with 1492 remaining. The craving is for an Eye Monster (eyemonster), which is shown as a bubble.\n\nWait, the board state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So there's an active craving for an Eye Monster. But the user just identified cell (3,3) as eyemonster_lvl1. However, the current board state shows that the cells are:\n\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN]\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (2,1) bone\n- (2,2) ribcage\n- (3,2) peasant (champion)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE]\n\nWait, the user's tool response after identifying cell (3,3) as eyemonster_lvl1. So now that cell is known. But the board state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So the craving is for an Eye Monster, which is a level 1? Or maybe it's a higher level.\n\nWait, the user's tool response shows that eyemonster_lvl1 can be merged to summon a higher level. So the current craving is for an Eye Monster, probably level 1. But the board state says \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat, but the current state might not have it.\n\nWait, looking at the Feats line: [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done). So"}
{"t": 1788691259.860236, "step": 7, "turn": 21, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_7", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_7", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: [(3, 3)]\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (6 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "proactive_identify_1788691187075", "function": {"name": "identify_item", "arguments": "{\"cells\": [[3, 3]]}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "proactive_identify_1788691187075", "content": "{\"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"eyemonster_lvl1\", \"cell\": [3, 3], \"merge_info\": \"two Eye Monster -> Eye Monster of the next level\", \"description\": \"Merge to summon a higher lvl Eye Monster.\"}]}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's see. The user provided the board state and then called identify_item on cell (3,3), which turned out to be eyemonster_lvl1.\n\nFirst, I need to check what the current board situation is. The board has several items. Let me list them again:\n\n- (0,0): coins_lvl2 (feed 5)\n- (0,1): coins_lvl1 (feed 2)\n- (0,2): manapool_lvl1 (feed 60, dmg 25)\n- (0,3): necromerger [UNKNOWN]\n- (1,1): gems_lvl1 (feed 2)\n- (1,2): cauldron [UNKNOWN]\n- (1,3): supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (2,0): bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5)\n- (2,1): bone (feed 1)\n- (2,2): ribcage (feed 2)\n- (3,2): peasant (champion) (feed 1)\n- (4,0): zombie_lvl5\n- (4,2): grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (4,3): grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (3,3): eyemonster_lvl1 (just identified)\n\nEmpty cells: (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\n\nThe user's previous tool call was to identify the unidentified cell (3,3), which is now confirmed as eyemonster_lvl1.\n\nNow, looking at the board state. The active feats include \"Build a Supply Cupboard\" which is done, so that's completed. The main focus seems to be on rune economy since the suggested direction is rune_economy.\n\nThe current craving is eyemonster (from the bubble), but the user has just identified an eyemonster_lvl1 at (3,3). Wait, the craving is for an Eye Monster, which matches the newly identified item. However, the board already has a level 1 Eye Monster? Or maybe the craving is for a higher level.\n\nWait, the get_board_state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So the current craving is to get an Eye Monster. Since there's now an eyemonster_lvl1 on the board, but the craving might be for a specific level. However, the user has just spawned or merged to get this"}
{"t": 1788691270.183937, "step": 7, "turn": 22, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: [(3, 3)]\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (6 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action.\n\n{\"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"eyemonster_lvl1\", \"cell\": [3, 3], \"merge_info\": \"two Eye Monster -> Eye Monster of the next level\", \"description\": \"Merge to summon a higher lvl Eye Monster.\"}]}"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1, 3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1, 3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788691369.807521, "step": 8, "turn": 23, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_8", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_8", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.64)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (5 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down step by step. First, I need to understand the current board state from the provided tool response.\n\nThe board has several items. Let me list out the key points:\n\n- **Occupied cells**: There are 13 occupied cells with their labels and statuses. Notable ones include:\n  - (0,0): coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n  - (0,1): coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n  - (0,2): manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25)\n  - (0,3): necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed]\n  - (1,3): supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n  - (2,1): bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n  - (2,2): ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n  - (3,2): peasant (champion)\n  - (4,2): grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n  - (4,3): grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE]\n\n- **Empty cells**: 4 empty cells: (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\n\n- **Best spawn**: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (5 empty)\n- **Mana**: ~100% full\n- **Satiety**: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\n- **Cravings**: eyemonster\n- **Feats**: Beat the Peasant twice (0/0), Merge things 250 times (0/0), Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster (0/0), Build a Supply Cupboard (done).\n\nThe user's instruction says to choose the single best move from the options: merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle.\n\nFirst, check for active cravings. The craving is \"eyemonster\". The current board has an eyeball (feed 1) and possibly other items that can lead to eyemonster. But the craving is for an Eye Monster, which might be a higher level. However, looking at the occupied cells, there's no eye monster yet. The supplycupboard_lvl1 spawns eyeball, which is part of the chain to get an Eye Monster"}
{"t": 1788691403.98494, "step": 8, "turn": 24, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_8", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_8", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.64)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (5 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state with all the occupied cells and their details. Let me go through each part step by step.\n\nFirst, the occupied cells:\n\n- (0,0): coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,1): coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,2): manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25)\n- (0,3): necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed]\n- (1,1): gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (1,2): cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed]\n- (1,3): supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (2,0): bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,1): bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,2): ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,3): eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n- (3,2): peasant (champion) (feed 1)\n- (4,0): zombie_lvl5\n- (4,2): grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (4,3): grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE]\n\nEmpty cells: (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\n\nBest spawn is supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3) which spawns eyeball. But wait, the user mentioned \"Best spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (5 empty)\". However, looking at the board state, there's a note that the mana bar is ~100% full, so spawning might not be the best idea here. Wait, but the user says \"Mana: ~100% full\" which means the mana bar is almost full, so collecting or feeding might be better.\n\nWait, the board has 5 empty cells. The supplycupboard_lvl1 can spawn eyeball, but it costs Slime. However, the mana bar is at 100%, so maybe spawning isn't the best move here. Let"}
{"t": 1788691413.729955, "step": 8, "turn": 25, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.64)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (5 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1, 3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1, 3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788691489.833212, "step": 9, "turn": 26, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_9", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_9", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.52)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.65)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.67)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.81, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (3 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: board_management (board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down step by step. The user provided the current board state after a get_board_state call. My job is to figure out the best move based on the rules and the given information.\n\nFirst, I need to look at the occupied cells and the hints provided. The board has 5 rows and 4 columns, so 20 cells total. There are 3 empty cells: (1,0), (3,0), (4,1). \n\nThe key points from the board state:\n\n- **Best merge hint**: eyeball (2,3) + (3,1). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE], so they can be merged. The merge would produce an Eye Monster, which is part of the craving mentioned (cravings: eyemonster).\n\n- **Craving**: The Devourer has a craving for an Eye Monster (lvl 5), but the current state shows \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat that's not completed. Wait, the board state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\", which probably means the current craving is for an Eye Monster.\n\n- **Feats**: The active feats include \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice\" (0/2), \"Merge things 250 times\" (0/250), and \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" (0/1). Also, \"Build a Supply Cupboard\" is done.\n\n- **Suggested direction**: board_management because the board is congested. So merging aggressively makes sense here.\n\nNow, looking at the merge hint: two eyeballs (2,3) and (3,1) can be merged. The Eye Monster is the next step in the chain. But wait, the craving is for an Eye Monster, so merging these two would fulfill part of the craving. However, the current state shows that the \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" feat is 0/0, which might mean it's not yet possible to have one on the board.\n\nWait, but the merge hint says \"Best merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\". So merging these two would create an Eye Monster. But the problem is, the current state shows that there are multiple eyeballs and other items. Let me check the item list:\n\n- (2,3) is eyeball (feed 1)\n- (3,1) is also eyeball (feed 1)\n\nSo merging two eyeb"}
{"t": 1788691524.56559, "step": 9, "turn": 27, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_9", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_9", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.52)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.65)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.67)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.81, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (3 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: board_management (board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's see. The user provided the current board state and wants me to decide the best move. Let me go through the details carefully.\n\nFirst, looking at the board state:\n\n- There are empty cells at (1,0), (3,0), (4,1). So the board isn't too congested, but there are three empty spots.\n- The \"Best merge\" hint is eyeball (2,3) + (3,1). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE], so merging them is possible. Let me check if they're the same item. The labels are both \"eyeball\", which is a creature. Wait, but in the list, (2,3) is eyeball (feed 1) and (3,1) is also eyeball (feed 1). So merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster? Wait, looking at the item glossary: supplycupboard_lvl1 spawns eyeinjar, but maybe the eyeball merges into something else. Wait, the user's item list shows that \"eyeball\" has a description: \"Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\" So merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster? Wait, no\u2014the chain is probably different. Wait, the user's item list says for \"eyeball\": merge to summon Eye in a Jar (eyeinjar). But maybe the Eye Monster is another item. Hmm.\n\nWait, the current board has (3,2) as peasant (champion), which is a champion. The Feats line mentions \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" So there's a feat to beat the Peasant twice. But the user's board state shows that the Peasant is on the board at (3,2). However, the current move options are about merging or spawning.\n\nThe Best merge hint is eyeball (2,3) + (3,1). Let me check if those two cells have the same item. Both are labeled as \"eyeball\" with feed 1. So they are identical. Merging them would create an Eye Monster? Wait, according to the item list: supplycupboard_lvl1 spawns eyeinjar, but maybe the eyeball merges into something else. Wait, the user's item list for \"eyeball\" says \"Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\" So merging two eyeballs would produce an Eye in a Jar (eyeinjar). But the Feats line has \"Own a"}
{"t": 1788691534.799191, "step": 9, "turn": 28, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.52)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.65)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.67)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.81, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 0.73, margin 0.20)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (3 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: board_management (board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [2, 3], \"b\": [3, 1]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [2, 3], \"b\": [3, 1]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788691638.1215758, "step": 10, "turn": 29, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_10", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_10", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.47)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.95, margin 0.72)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.77, margin 0.48)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (4 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down step by step. First, I need to understand the current board state from the provided tool response.\n\nThe board has several items. Let me list out the key points:\n\n- **Occupied cells**: There are 15 occupied cells with their labels and statuses. Notable ones include:\n  - (0,0): coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n  - (0,1): coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n  - (0,2): manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25)\n  - (0,3): necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed]\n  - (1,3): supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n  - (2,1): bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n  - (2,2): ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n  - (3,2): peasant (champion)\n  - (4,2): grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n  - (4,3): grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE]\n\n- **Empty cells**: 4 empty cells: (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1)\n\n- **Best spawn**: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) with 4 empty cells.\n\n- **Mana bar**: ~100% full.\n\n- **Satiety**: 508/2000 (1492 remaining).\n\n- **Cravings**: eyemonster.\n\n- **Feats**: The main active feat is \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" which is at 0/0. Also, there's a \"Build a Supply Cupboard\" which is done.\n\nThe user's strategy is to prioritize rune_economy since the rune balances are low. But looking at the board, the current state has a craving for an Eye Monster (eyemonster), which is a high-value item. However, the supplycupboard_lvl1 can spawn eyeball, which is part of the chain to get the Eye Monster.\n\nWait, the supplycupboard_LVL1 spawns eyeball, which is then used to make eyeinajar, and eventually the Eye Monster. But the current craving is for eyemonster, so maybe we need to build up the chain.\n\nBut looking"}
{"t": 1788691673.5364301, "step": 10, "turn": 30, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_10", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_10", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.47)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.95, margin 0.72)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.77, margin 0.48)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (4 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state with all the occupied cells and their details. Let me go through each part step by step.\n\nFirst, the occupied cells:\n\n- (0,0) is coins_lvl2 (feed 5), which is FEEDABLE.\n- (0,1) is coins_lvl1 (feed 2), also FEEDABLE.\n- (0,2) is manapool_lvl1 (feed 60, dmg 25). This is a station, but it's not the NecroMerger, so maybe it can be merged? Wait, no\u2014manapool is a station, but the rules say stations can be merged. Wait, the user mentioned that merging stations is normal and valid. So manapool_lvl1 can merge with another manapool_lvl1 to become lvl2.\n\nBut looking at the board, there's only one manapool_lvl1 here. So no merge possible for that.\n\n- (0,3) is necromerger, which is unknown but shouldn't be fed.\n- (1,3) is supplycupboard_lvl1, which is a spawn station. It can spawn eyeball, eyeinjar, etc., but it's already on the board. Wait, the user says \"supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\". So tapping it would spawn an item.\n\n- (2,0) is bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5), FEEDABLE.\n- (2,1) is bone (feed 1), FEEDABLE.\n- (2,2) is ribcage (feed 2), FEEDABLE.\n- (3,2) is peasant (champion), which is a champion. So if there's a creature with dmg N, we can attack it.\n\n- (4,0) is zombie_lvl5, which is a high-level item. It's max level? Wait, the user says \"zombie_lvl5\" but in the wiki, maybe it's not max. But according to the board state, it's listed as score 1.00, margin 0.55. Maybe it's a valid item.\n\n- (4,2) is grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE], which can spawn bone.\n- (4,3) is grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE], which can spawn bone"}
{"t": 1788691683.512624, "step": 10, "turn": 31, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.47)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.95, margin 0.72)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.77, margin 0.48)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.83, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 (1,3) -> eyeball (costs Slime) (4 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: rune_economy (rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds \u2014 consider set_strategy with target_family 'grave').\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
