pup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item peasant (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}, "id": "ZBSN5S6k1VjF4raQ3RsJkUYUzkFnqaOR"}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "ZBSN5S6k1VjF4raQ3RsJkUYUzkFnqaOR", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.62)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.64)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.82, margin 0.46)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.56)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.74, margin 0.44)\n- (3,2) peasant (champion) (feed 1) (score 0.95, margin 0.66)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.77, margin 0.48)\n- (4,0) zombie_lvl5 (score 1.00, margin 0.55)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (3 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 508/2000 (1492 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: board_management (board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (4,2) grave_lvl1 \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's see. The user provided the current board state and wants me to decide the best move. Let me go through the details carefully.\n\nFirst, looking at the board state:\n\n- There are 5 rows and 4 columns, so 20 cells total. Empty cells are (1,0), (3,0), (4,1) \u2014 that's three empty spots.\n- The \"Best merge\" hint is eyeball (2,3) + (3,3). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE], so they can be merged. But wait, the merge chain for eyeball: from the item list, eyeball is part of the supplycupboard chain. Wait, the user mentioned that merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster? Let me check the item info.\n\nWait, in the items learned section, there's \"Item eyeball (popup)\" which says \"Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\" But the supplycupboard levels spawn eyeinajar. Hmm, maybe the chain is different. Wait, the user has a list of items:\n\n- Item eyeball: feed value 1, merge to summon Eye in a Jar.\n- Item eyeinajar: feed value 2, merge to summon Eye Monster.\n\nSo merging two eyeballs would make an eyeinajar? But the board state shows (3,3) is eyeball (feed 1), and (2,3) is also eyeball. Wait, no: looking at the occupied cells:\n\n(2,3) is eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n(3,3) is eyeball (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n\nWait, but the \"Best merge\" hint says eyeball (2,3)+(3,3). So merging two eyeballs. But according to the item info, merging two eyeballs would create an eyeinajar? Wait, no: the supplycupboard levels spawn eyeinajar. Let me check the wiki items.\n\nIn the item list:\n\n- Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn): spawns eyeinajar.\n- Item eyeball (popup): \"Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\" So maybe merging two eyeballs gives an eyeinajar, which then can be merged into an Eye Monster. But the user's board state shows that there's an eyeinajar at (3,1) and (3,2) is peasant (champion). Wait, no: (3,1)"}
