ed cells. There are several items here. Let me check for possible merges. The board has 5 rows x 4 columns, so 20 cells total. Empty cells are (1,0), (3,0), (4,1). \n\nThe user mentioned \"Best feed: eyeinajar (3,1) (feed 2) (fits 1492 remaining)\". So the Devourer's satiety is 508/2000 with 1492 remaining. The current craving is for an Eye Monster, which is probably a higher level item. But the best feed hint points to eyeinajar at (3,1), which has a feed value of 2. However, feeding it might not be optimal if there's a better use.\n\nWait, the Feats line says \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" and \"Build a Supply Cupboard\" is done. The suggested direction is board_management because the board is congested. So merging aggressively makes sense here.\n\nLooking at the items: (2,1) is bone (feed 1), (2,2) is ribcage (feed 2). Bone can merge into ribcage. If there's a ribcage, then maybe two ribcages can merge into a skeleton. But the current board has a ribcage at (2,2) and a bone at (2,1). Wait, but the user mentioned \"Best merge: ...\" in the tool results. Let me check again.\n\nWait, the tool result says \"Best feed: eyeinajar (3,1) (feed 2) (fits 1492 remaining)\". But there's also a Best spawn hint. The valid spawns are supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3) and grave_lvl1 at (4,2), grave_lvl3 at (4,3). \n\nBut the board is congested with empty cells: three empty spots. However, the user's suggested direction is board_management, which means merging aggressively. But there's a problem: the current board has some items that can be merged. Let's see.\n\nLooking at the occupied cells:\n\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1)\n- (2,2"}
