plycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_40", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_40", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.60)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down step by step. The user provided the current board state after calling get_board_state. My job is to figure out the best move based on the rules and the given information.\n\nFirst, I need to look at the occupied cells and their statuses. Let me list out the key points from the board state:\n\n- There are empty cells: (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1). So 5 empty spots.\n- The \"Best merge\" hint is eyeball (2,3) + (3,3). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE], so they can be merged. Wait, but the merge chain for eyeball is to summon an Eye Monster. But the user's board state shows that there's a craving for an Eye Monster (since the Cravings bubble says \"eyemonster\"). \n\nWait, the Feats line mentions \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat, but it's not completed yet. However, the current board has two eyeballs at (2,3) and (3,3). The Best merge hint is to merge those two. But why would merging them be the best move?\n\nWait, the craving is for an Eye Monster. So if we have two eyeballs, merging them would create an Eye Monster. But the problem is, the current state shows that the Feats line has \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat, but it's at 0/0. However, the user might not have reached level 5 yet. Wait, the board state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So maybe the craving is for the base Eye Monster, not the level 5.\n\nWait, the merge chain for eyeball: according to the item glossary, supplycupboard_lvl1 spawns eyeball, and then merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster. But the user's board has two eyeballs (at (2,3) and (3,3)), so merging them would give an Eye Monster. However, the craving is for \"eyemonster\", which might be the base version.\n\nBut the Feats line says \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat. So maybe the user needs to get to level 5. But the current board state shows that there's no level 5 Eye Monster yet. However, the Best merge hint is for merging two eyeballs into an Eye"}
{"t": 1788696199.536337, "step": 40, "turn": 123, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_40", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_40", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.60)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down. The user provided the board state after a get_board_state call. I need to figure out the best move based on the rules and the current situation.\n\nFirst, looking at the occupied cells. There are several items here. Let me check for possible merges. The \"Best merge\" hint says eyeball (2,3) + (3,3). Both are eyeballs, so merging them would create an Eye Monster. But wait, the craving is for an Eye Monster (eyemonster), which is probably a level 1 or higher. Since the user has a craving, feeding the exact item might be better, but the hint says to merge.\n\nWait, the Feats line mentions \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat, but it's not completed yet. The current state shows that the craving is for an Eye Monster, so maybe merging two eyeballs would help progress towards that. But the user also has a champion present (since the suggested direction is champion_combat), which might mean there's a Peasant or other champion on the board.\n\nWait, the empty cells are (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1). The board is 5x4, so 20 cells total. There are 14 occupied cells listed here, so 6 empty? Wait, no: the user says \"Empty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\". So 5 empty cells.\n\nThe Best merge hint is eyeball (2,3) and (3,3). Both are eyeballs. Merging them would create an Eye Monster. But the craving is for an Eye Monster, so maybe feeding it would be better. However, the Feats line says \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" which might require multiple merges.\n\nWait, but the current state shows that the user has two eyeballs (2,3) and (3,3). Merging them would give an Eye Monster. But the craving is for an Eye Monster, so maybe feeding it would count towards the craving. However, the hint says \"Best merge\" is this pair.\n\nBut the user also has a champion present (since the suggested direction is champion_combat), which might mean they need to attack. The Feats line mentions \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" So"}
{"t": 1788696209.720662, "step": 40, "turn": 124, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.97, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.61)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.60)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [2, 3], \"b\": [3, 3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [2, 3], \"b\": [3, 3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788696296.691673, "step": 41, "turn": 125, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Call get_board_state now. Emit ONLY the tool call."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}, "id": "aw2nijVHRal4gGnLfpEE4RvLSVjZyrA7"}], "reasoning": "Okay, the user is asking me to call the get_board_state function. Let me check the tools provided.\n\nThe available tool is get_board_state, which requires no parameters. The user says to emit only the tool call, so I need to make sure I don't add any extra text. Just the tool_call with the correct name and arguments.\n\nWait, the function has an empty parameters object. So the arguments should be an empty JSON object. Let me confirm: the parameters section says \"properties\": {} and \"required\": [], so yes, no arguments needed.\n\nSo the correct tool call is {\"name\": \"get_board_state\", \"arguments\": {}}. I need to wrap this in the tool_call XML tags as specified. No other functions are available here, so that's the only one to use.\n"}
{"t": 1788696325.066355, "step": 41, "turn": 126, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}, "id": "aw2nijVHRal4gGnLfpEE4RvLSVjZyrA7"}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "aw2nijVHRal4gGnLfpEE4RvLSVjZyrA7", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.50)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (6 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune (6 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state. Let me parse through it carefully.\n\nOccupied cells:\n- (0,0): coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,1): coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,2): manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,3): necromerger [UNKNOWN] \u2014 don't feed\n- (1,1): gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (1,2): cauldron [UNKNOWN] \u2014 don't feed\n- (1,3): supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (2,0): bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,1): bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,2): ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (3,2): icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN] \u2014 but it's spawnable\n- (3,3): eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (4,2): grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (4,3): grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE]\n\nEmpty cells: (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1) \u2014 6 empty.\n\nBest spawn is icebox_unopened at (3,2) which can spawn icerune/poisonrune. But the user also has a supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3). Wait, but the Best spawn hint says icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune with 6 empty cells.\n\nWait, the Feats line mentions \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" which is a champion combat feat. The board state shows that there's a champion present (since the suggested direction is champion_combat). So the current situation has a Peasant or similar champion on the board.\n\nLooking at the occupied cells, there's no explicit mention of a champion cell. Wait, but the Feats line says \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" which implies"}
{"t": 1788696359.8121972, "step": 41, "turn": 127, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}, "id": "aw2nijVHRal4gGnLfpEE4RvLSVjZyrA7"}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "aw2nijVHRal4gGnLfpEE4RvLSVjZyrA7", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.50)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (6 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune (6 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state with all the occupied cells and their labels. Let me go through each part step by step.\n\nFirst, the occupied cells:\n\n- (0,0): coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,1): coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,2): manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,3): necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (can't feed)\n- (1,1): gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (1,2): cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed]\n- (1,3): supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (2,0): bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,1): bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,2): ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (3,2): icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE]\n- (3,3): eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (4,2): grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (4,3): grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE]\n\nEmpty cells: (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1) \u2014 6 empty cells.\n\nThe best spawn hint is icebox_unopened at (3,2) which can spawn icerune/poisonrune. But wait, the user mentioned that the board has a champion present, so maybe we should prioritize attacking the champion. However, looking at the Feats line: \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" and \"Build a Supply Cupboard\" is done.\n\nWait, the current craving is eyemonster (from the bubble). The board state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So we need to feed an Eye Monster. But the existing items on the board don't include an Eye Monster. However, there's a supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3"}
{"t": 1788696369.786753, "step": 41, "turn": 128, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.90, margin 0.51)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.50)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (6 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune (6 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788696479.985423, "step": 42, "turn": 129, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_42", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_42", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.92, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.66)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.57)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune (5 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state. Let me parse through all the details.\n\nFirst, the occupied cells: there are several items listed with their types, feed values, and whether they're feedable or spawnable. The empty cells are (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1) \u2014 so 5 empty spots. \n\nThe Feats line says \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" which is a champion combat feat. The bottom bar shows that the Shop is locked, but the Station and Queue are unlocked. Also, there's a Best spawn hint for icebox_unopened at (3,2), which can spawn icerune/poisonrune.\n\nWait, the Feats line mentions \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" as a neutral feat. But the user also has a champion present? Wait, the board state says \"Suggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\" So there's a champion on the board, probably The Peasant.\n\nLooking at the occupied cells, there's a necromerger at (0,3), which is unknown but not feedable. There's also a supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3), which is spawnable. But the Best spawn hint points to icebox_unopened at (3,2). \n\nWait, the Feats line says \"Build a Supply Cupboard.\" is done. So maybe that's already completed. The active feat is \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice.\" which needs two attacks on the Peasant.\n\nNow, looking for high-damage minions to attack the Peasant. The board has several items with damage values. For example, manapool_lvl1 at (0,2) has dmg 25. But wait, the description says \"manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25)\" \u2014 so it's a creature that can attack. Similarly, necromancer (but not listed here), but maybe other items.\n\nWait, in the occupied cells, there's manapool_lvl1 at (0,2) with dmg 25. Also, coins_lvl2 and others. But the highest damage might be from the skeleton or something else. Wait, looking at the list:\n\n- (0,"}
{"t": 1788696514.616311, "step": 42, "turn": 130, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_42", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_42", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.92, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.66)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.57)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune (5 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state with all the occupied cells and their labels. Let me go through each part step by step.\n\nFirst, the empty cells are (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1). There are 5 empty cells, which is a bit sparse but not too bad. The board has some spawnable stations: supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3), icebox_unopened at (3,2), and grave_lvl1 and grave_lvl3 at (4,2) and (4,3). \n\nThe \"Best spawn\" hint says icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune with 5 empty cells. But wait, the user mentioned that the board has 5 empty cells, so spawning from the icebox would use one of them. However, the Feats line shows \"Build a Supply Cupboard\" is done, which might mean they already have it. Wait, the supplycupboard_lvl1 is on the board at (1,3), but maybe it's a different level.\n\nWait, looking at the occupied cells: there's a supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3). The Feats line says \"Build a Supply Cupboard\" is done, so maybe they already built it. But the user might have multiple levels. Hmm, perhaps the supplycupboard is already built, but the level here is lvl1.\n\nNow, the main thing is to check what's the best move. Let's see the hints and the active feats.\n\nThe Feats line mentions \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice\" (0/0), which is a combat feat. The user also has a craving for an Eye Monster (eyemonster). But the board state shows that there's a supplycupboard_lvl1, which spawns eyeball or eyeinajar. Wait, the supplycupboard_LVL1 spawns eyeball, but the craving is for an Eye Monster. Maybe the Eye Monster is a higher level.\n\nWait, looking at the item list: \"eyeinajar\" (feed 2) is present at (3,3). The supplycupboard_lvl1 spawns eyeball, which is feed value 15. But the craving is for an Eye Monster, which might be from merging eyeinajar or something"}
{"t": 1788696524.6418822, "step": 42, "turn": 131, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.92, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.66)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.57)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune (5 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"spawn\", \"cell\": [1,3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788696634.608163, "step": 43, "turn": 132, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_43", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_43", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.92, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.66)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down step by step. The user provided the current board state, and I need to figure out the best move based on the rules and the given information.\n\nFirst, looking at the board state:\n\n- There are empty cells: (1,0), (3,0), (4,0), (4,1). So there's space available.\n- The \"Best merge\" hint is eyeball (2,3) + (3,1). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE], so they can be merged. But wait, the merge chain for eyeball: from the item list, eyeball is part of the Eye Monster chain. The user mentioned that merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster. Wait, but the board has two eyeballs at (2,3) and (3,1). Let me check the item descriptions.\n\nLooking at the items:\n- (2,3) is eyeball (feed 15)\n- (3,1) is also eyeball (feed 15)\n\nSo merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster. The craving is for eyemonster, which is a level 1 Eye Monster. Since the craving is active, merging these two might be beneficial because it's part of fulfilling the craving.\n\nWait, the craving is \"eyemonster\" (probably level 1), so having two eyeballs would merge into an Eye Monster, which would count toward the craving. But the user mentioned that feeding the craved item at the exact level counts toward the quota. However, merging precursors (like eyeball) towards the craving is better than feeding them.\n\nBut according to the rules: \"Never feed a same-family LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally.\" So if the craving is for Eye Monster (lvl 1), then the precursors are lower levels. But in this case, the eyeball is the precursor to Eye Monster. So merging two eyeballs would create the Eye Monster, which would fulfill the craving.\n\nBut the current state shows that there's a \"Best merge\" hint for those two eyeballs. The user should merge them because it's the highest priority move as per the hint. Also, the Feats line mentions \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice\" but it's 0/0, so maybe not relevant here.\n\nWait, the board has an empty cell (4,1), which is a possible spawn"}
{"t": 1788696669.394071, "step": 43, "turn": 133, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_43", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_43", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.92, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.66)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down. The user provided the current board state after a get_board_state call. My job is to figure out the best move based on the rules and the given data.\n\nFirst, looking at the occupied cells. There are several items here. The key points from the board state:\n\n- Empty cells: (1,0), (3,0), (4,0), (4,1) \u2014 four empty spots.\n- Best merge hint is eyeball (2,3) and (3,1). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE], so they can be merged. Wait, but the merge hint says \"Best merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\". Let me check if those two are the same item. The labels are both \"eyeball\" with feed 15 each. So merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster? But the user's past learnings mention that Eye Monster is a higher level. Wait, the merge chain for eyeball: according to the item glossary, supplycupboard_lvl1 spawns eyeball, and then maybe eyeinajar. But the merge chain for eyeball itself isn't listed here. Wait, the user provided some item info: \"Item eyeball (popup)\" says feed value 15, description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar. So merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster? Or maybe it's part of a chain.\n\nWait, the board state shows two eyeballs at (2,3) and (3,1). The Best merge hint is for those two. But according to the rules, merging identical items. Since both are eyeball, they can be merged. However, the user's past learnings mention that \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" is a feat, but the current board has eyeballs. Wait, maybe merging two eyeballs creates an Eye Monster (lvl1?), which would then be part of the chain.\n\nBut the problem is: the Best merge hint is given as \"eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\". So the bot suggests merging those two. But why? Let's check if there's a craving. The board state says Cravings (bubble): eyemonster. So the current craving is for an Eye Monster. Which would be the next level up from eyeball. So merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster, which would fulfill the craving.\n\nWait, but the user's item glossary shows that"}
{"t": 1788696679.7476852, "step": 43, "turn": 134, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.92, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.71)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.66)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.91, margin 0.54)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.92, margin 0.55)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (4 of 20): (1,0), (3,0), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeball (2,3)+(3,1)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeball (2,3)+(3,1) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [2, 3], \"b\": [3, 1]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [2, 3], \"b\": [3, 1]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788696788.431021, "step": 44, "turn": 135, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_44", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_44", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.52)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.86, margin 0.10)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down step by step. The user provided the current board state, and I need to figure out the best move based on the rules and the given information.\n\nFirst, looking at the occupied cells:\n\n- There are two eyeinajar (3,1) and (3,3). The Best merge hint says to merge these two. Since they're both eyeinajar, which is a creature, merging them would create an Eye Monster. But wait, the Feats line mentions \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat, but it's currently at 0/0. However, the current state shows that there's a craving for an eyemonster (from the Cravings bubble). \n\nWait, the board state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So the game is craving an Eye Monster. The eyeinajar is a lower level item (feed 2), and merging two of them would create an Eye Monster. But according to the merge chain, the Eye Monster is the next level after eyeinajar. Let me check the item list: \"eyeinajar\" has a description that says \"Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\" So yes, merging two eyeinajar should give an Eye Monster.\n\nNow, the Feats line mentions \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" but it's not completed yet. However, the current state shows that there's a craving for an eyemonster, which is probably the next step. But the user's board has two eyeinajar, so merging them would fulfill the craving. Wait, but the craving might be for a specific level. The problem says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\" \u2014 maybe it's the base level, and the exact level isn't specified here.\n\nBut according to the rules, when there's an active craving, you should feed the exact level item. However, in this case, the craving is for an Eye Monster, which would be the result of merging two eyeinajar. So if we merge them, we get the Eye Monster, which would fulfill the craving. But wait, the Feats line says \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" \u2014 but maybe the current level is lower.\n\nWait, the user's board state shows that there are two eyeinajar (3,1) and (3,3). The Best merge hint is to merge those two. So merging them would create an Eye Monster. But the Feats line says \"Own a lvl "}
{"t": 1788696823.4129841, "step": 44, "turn": 136, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_44", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_44", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.52)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.86, margin 0.10)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}, {"role": "user", "content": "If you need several of these, call them ALL in this round (multiple tool calls at once) instead of one per round."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's break this down. The user provided the board state after a get_board_state call. I need to figure out the best move based on the rules and the current situation.\n\nFirst, looking at the occupied cells. There are several items here. Let me check for possible merges. The \"Best merge\" hint says eyeinajar (3,1) + (3,3). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE], so they can be merged. Merging two eyeinajar would create a higher level Eye Monster, which is part of the craving. Wait, the craving is for an Eye Monster, and the current cells are eyeinajar (which is a lower level). But according to the merge chain, maybe merging two eyeinajar gives a higher level. However, the user's past learnings mention that Eye Monster is craved, so merging these might help fulfill the craving.\n\nWait, the Feats line says \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" but it's 0/0. So maybe the current state has some eyeinajar, and merging them would progress towards the Eye Monster. But the hint says Best merge is eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3). Let me check if those are the same item. Both are eyeinajar, so yes, they can be merged.\n\nBut wait, the user's strategy should prioritize the active feats. The Feats line has \"Beat the Peasant in combat twice\" which is 0/0, and \"Build a Supply Cupboard\" which is done. So maybe the main focus is on the craving. Since the craving is for an Eye Monster, merging two eyeinajar would be a step towards that. However, the current cells are both eyeinajar (feed 2 each), so merging them would create a higher level Eye Monster. But according to the wiki, the merge chain for eyeinajar is probably into an Eye Monster. Let me check the item list: \"eyeinajar\" has a description that says \"Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\" So yes, two eyeinajar would make an Eye Monster.\n\nBut wait, the user's past learnings mention that the Eye Monster is craved. The current craving is \"eyemonster\", so merging these two would be towards fulfilling that craving. However, the Feats line also has \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" which might be a different feat. But since the craving is active, feeding or merging towards it is important.\n\nBut"}
{"t": 1788696833.452672, "step": 44, "turn": 137, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object."}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}, {"type": "text", "text": "Tool results:\nOccupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.91, margin 0.52)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.72)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.55)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.96, margin 0.68)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (3,1) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.86, margin 0.10)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeinajar (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.70, margin 0.41)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (5 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest merge: eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid merges: merge eyeinajar (3,1)+(3,3) | Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [3, 1], \"b\": [3, 3]}"}], "reply": "{\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [3, 1], \"b\": [3, 3]}", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": null}
{"t": 1788696941.779048, "step": 45, "turn": 138, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl2 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl3 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl4 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl5 -> eyeball, eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item bloodrune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n- edge: bloodrune -> bigger pile\n  [source: popup]\n## Item bone (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1\n- description: Merge to summon a Rib Cage.\n- edge: two Bone -> Rib Cage\n- edge: bone -> rib cage\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item coins_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 30\n- max_level: true\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item gems_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- description: Spawns bone/ribcage/zombie when tapped.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icebox_unopened (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to open.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerune_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 12\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item lockedchest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to watch an advert to unlock this Valuable Chest.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapool_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapot_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- description: Increases Mana Cap. Merge to lvl up.\n- edge: Mana Cap +2000\n  [source: popup]\n## Item manapotion_lvl3 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 22\n- max_level: true\n- description: Feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "[image]"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "This is the current board. The board state is already provided below (see Tool results) \u2014 decide the single best move and reply with ONLY a valid JSON action (merge, spawn, feed, attack, collect, or idle). There are no tools in this round \u2014 never emit a tool call or a tool name as the action."}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"type": "function", "id": "direct_45", "function": {"name": "get_board_state", "arguments": "{}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "direct_45", "content": "Occupied cells (template bank labels):\n- (0,0) coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.96, margin 0.63)\n- (0,1) coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.60)\n- (0,2) manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) (score 0.92, margin 0.53)\n- (0,3) necromerger [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 0.97, margin 0.68)\n- (1,1) gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.56)\n- (1,2) cauldron [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] (score 1.00, margin 0.72)\n- (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.69)\n- (2,0) bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.54)\n- (2,1) bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.99, margin 0.57)\n- (2,2) ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.57)\n- (3,2) icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN VALUE \u2014 do not feed] [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.93, margin 0.67)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.58)\n- (4,2) grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.84, margin 0.48)\n- (4,3) grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE] (score 0.98, margin 0.69)\nUnidentified occupied cells: []\nEmpty cells (6 of 20): (1,0), (2,3), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1)\nBest spawn: icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune (6 empty)\nMana: ~100% full\nSatiety: 578/2000 (1422 remaining)\nCravings (bubble): eyemonster\nBottom bar: unlocked feats,station,queue(reward),shop  locked spellbook\nFeats (tier 5): [neutral] Beat the Peasant in combat twice. (0/0 Feats Completed); [merge] Merge things 250 times. (0/0) [other]; [merge] Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster. (0/0) [other]; Build a Supply Cupboard. (done).\nSuggested direction: champion_combat (champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack).\nChoose ONLY from: Valid spawns: spawn (1,3) supplycupboard_lvl1; spawn (3,2) icebox_unopened \u2014 do NOT repeat any rejected move.\nDecision checklist: 1. Pick ONLY a move from the Choose ONLY from line (or a Best hint); prefer [FEEDABLE]/[SPAWNABLE] cells. 2. Never repeat a rejected move; never merge [NEVER MERGE] cells; never output a tool name. 3. Reply with ONLY the JSON action."}], "reply": "", "tool_calls": null, "reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out the best move here. First, I need to look at the board state provided.\n\nThe user has given me the current board state. Let me parse through it carefully.\n\nOccupied cells:\n- (0,0): coins_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,1): coins_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,2): manapool_lvl1 (feed 60) (dmg 25) [FEEDABLE]\n- (0,3): necromerger [UNKNOWN] \u2014 don't feed\n- (1,1): gems_lvl1 (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (1,2): cauldron [UNKNOWN] \u2014 don't feed\n- (1,3): supplycupboard_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (2,0): bloodrune_lvl2 (feed 5) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,1): bone (feed 1) [FEEDABLE]\n- (2,2): ribcage (feed 2) [FEEDABLE]\n- (3,2): icebox_unopened [UNKNOWN] \u2014 but it's spawnable\n- (3,3): eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE]\n- (4,2): grave_lvl1 [SPAWNABLE]\n- (4,3): grave_lvl3 [SPAWNABLE]\n\nEmpty cells: 6 of them. The best spawn hint is icebox_unopened at (3,2), which can spawn icerune/poisonrune. But wait, the user mentioned \"Best spawn: icebox_unopened (3,2) -> icerune/poisonrune (6 empty)\".\n\nWait, but there's also a supplycupboard_lvl1 at (1,3). However, the Feats line says \"Build a Supply Cupboard. (done)\", so that feat is already completed. So maybe the supplycupboard isn't needed anymore.\n\nThe current craving is eyemonster. The user has an eyeball at (3,3), which is feedable. But the craving is for an Eye Monster, which is probably from merging eyeinjar or something else. Wait, the supplycupboard spawns eyeball, but the craving is for eyemonster.\n\nWait, looking at the item list: there's an eyeball (feed 15)"}
{"t": 1788696976.556213, "step": 45, "turn": 139, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the brain of a bot playing NecroMerger on a 5x4 board.\nThe screenshot is 1280x2856 pixels, full emulator frame.\nBoard geometry: the board occupies pixels x=184-1096, y=1192-2332;\n5 rows x 4 columns, each cell 228px square. Top-left cell is (0,0), top-right (0,3),\nbottom-left (4,0), bottom-right (4,3). The Devourer's mouth is above the board at ~(642,923).\nRules:\n- Two identical items merge into one of the next level (e.g. zombie_lvl1 + zombie_lvl1 -> zombie_lvl2).\n- The LEVEL is part of an item's identity: creatures of the SAME type but DIFFERENT\n  levels are DIFFERENT items and NEVER merge (skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl2 is INVALID;\n  only two cells with the SAME id, like skeleton_lvl1 + skeleton_lvl1, merge). The\n  `get_board_state` labels (e.g. `skeleton_lvl1`) carry the exact level \u2014 trust the\n  label, not what the sprites look like.\n- MAX-LEVEL items: every item type has a TOP level. A max-level item's\n  info popup says only \"Feed to the Devourer.\" and has NO \"merge\" line \u2014\n  it can never merge again. When `get_board_state` marks a cell\n  `(max level)`, do NOT try to merge two of them \u2014 the game refuses.\n   Feeding one yields good food, but feeding is NOT its only use: max-level\n   creatures GENERATE RESOURCES (Mana, Slime, Darkness) while on the board\n   (higher levels generate more). Decide per situation: feed for Food/space\n   when needed; keep high-level generators when resource income matters.\n- SPAWNING \u2014 GRAVE: a Grave spawns bone/ribcage when tapped \u2014 it costs Mana\n  (the amount grows with the station's level) and silently does nothing when\n  the bar is empty, so do NOT spawn the grave when `get_board_state` shows\n  `Mana: (bar not visible)` or a low percent \u2014 collect instead. Spawning the\n  grave ALSO needs an EMPTY board cell: when `get_board_state` shows 0 empty\n  cells, spawns silently no-op \u2014 free a cell first (merge two of the same to\n  combine, or feed a non-critical creature to clear a slot). A FULL Mana bar\n  is exactly when you SHOULD spawn the grave: spawning spends the bar down.\n  (Other stations spawn from different Resources: a Slime Vat spawns with\n  Slime, a Dark Stores with Darkness. The Mana Pool, Slime Vat, and Dark\n  Stores are NOT spawn stations \u2014 they are Resource-CAPACITY stations that\n  boost the max of their Resource; bought with Runes like any other station.)\n- SPAWNING \u2014 ICE CHEST (and other chests): an Ice Chest (the `icebox` you see\n  on the board) spawns one random rune per tap \u2014 see your item glossary for\n  the exact `spawn` chain and current rates. It costs NO Resource (Mana,\n  Slime, or Darkness \u2014 the bar at the top of the lair), but each spawned\n  rune occupies a board cell, and the chest is FINITE USES (e.g. the\n  standard icebox has 5 uses). The `Open a chest.` feat counts each tap as\n  one open. Merge the rune stacks up to max level (icerune lvl1 -> lvl2 -> lvl3\n  max; poison has its own chain), then FEED the max-level stack \u2014 that grants\n  the corresponding Ice / Poison / Blood / Moon / Death Rune currency (NOT\n  food). That's the primary way to gather the 5 station-buying currencies\n  (the Shop also sells Runes for Gold/Gems, but the Shop isn't available\n  on the current save). NEVER feed a Rune (or Coin) stack below max level \u2014\n  the validator refuses `feed` on sub-max income stacks when any other\n  feedable exists; merge the stack up first so the per-feed payout is\n  the largest (icerune lvl3 grants 12 vs lvl1's 2; coin lvl4 grants 30\n  vs lvl1's 2).\n   WHEN to tap a chest: only when the rune feeds a stack that reaches max\n   level and gets fed within a few steps \u2014 a new stack, a mergeable stack,\n   or one or two merges from max. Do NOT tap just because uses remain:\n   runes accumulate faster than they merge, and each tap costs a cell.\n   Never tap when the board is full of `(max level)` items.\n- RESOURCE BAR: `get_board_state` shows the current Resource fill as\n  `Mana: ~N% full` (the only Resource bar visible on the lair for now \u2014\n  Slime and Darkness bars appear later when Slime Vat / Dark Stores are\n  built, and follow the same read convention). Do NOT `collect` when the\n  bar is `~100% full` \u2014 the tap is wasted. (Spawn/merge/feed instead \u2014\n  a full bar is a signal to spend the surplus.)\n- Feed a creature to the Devourer to gain food. When `get_board_state` labels a\n  cell as `(feed N)`, that N is the food value that creature yields when fed\n  (read from the in-game popup; see your item glossary for recorded values).\n  When choosing what to feed, prefer the lowest-value creature you don't\n  need (keep high-value/better items for merging or a future craving).\n- SATIETY: the Devourer's satiety bar shows how much more food is needed before\n  it levels up (`get_board_state` shows `Satiety: X/M (R remaining)` when it can\n  be read). Feeding an item whose `(feed N)` is LARGER than R wastes food \u2014 the\n  excess is lost and the game warns. Tolerance is up to ~10% of M (the safety\n  margin); beyond that it counts as waste. So feed only items whose feed\n  value fits R. Among fitting items, pick the SMALLEST one \u2014 feed value\n  scales non-linearly (a ribcage is worth more than the two bones that\n  create it, and a Skeleton L3 is worth more than the two L2s that merge\n  into it), so the smallest fitting item minimizes value destruction\n  while still making progress toward the level-up. Do NOT sacrifice a\n  high-level / resource-generating monster just to fill a small gap. If\n  nothing fits even with the tolerance, don't feed at all \u2014 spawn instead\n  (or `attack` if a champion is on the board).\n- CRAVING OVERFLOW: each feed of a craving's required item counts toward\n  its quota (e.g. a `Rib Cage (lvl 1) 0/2` craving needs 2 ribcage feeds);\n  the Food bonus is granted ONCE when the craving is FULFILLED (the final\n  feed pays out the bonus on top of the item's normal food). Feeding the\n  craved item into a nearly-full bar can therefore waste that big bonus:\n  if the bar's R is smaller than the item's `(feed N)` (or so close that\n  the final-completion bonus would push the total over the tolerance),\n  do NOT feed it now \u2014 the craving persists, so PREFER SPAWNING from a\n  spawn station to rebuild the craved item (the grave is the most common\n  source; some cravings come from chests, Lectern, or other stations) and\n  feed it after the bar resets on a level-up. A `Best spawn:` hint is shown\n  in that case. Never waste the completion bonus on an overflowing bar.\n- FEED-TO-PROGRESS: FEEDING the Devourer is how you advance \u2014 its level rises\n  with food, and every level unlocks something (Tier-1 uncrates the Devourer;\n  Lvl 3 unlocks cravings; Lvl 4+ drop ice chests; Lvl 5+ starts the Peasant;\n  Lvl 7+ grows the lair; the per-tier feat `Reach Devourer level N` is your\n  barometer of how close the next tier is). When NO merge is possible (no\n  `Best merge:` line) and there is no craving to feed, feed a NON-CRITICAL\n  creature to keep progressing instead of only spawning: prefer the CHEAPEST\n  fitting creature by `(feed N)` (per the glossary, bone=1, ribcage=5,\n  skeleton_lvl1=10 \u2014 these are the skeleton-chain bases, not needed for a\n  pending merge). `(max level)` items and HIGH-VALUE creatures are RESOURCE\n  GENERATORS (they passively make their Resource \u2014 Mana/Slime/Darkness \u2014\n  higher levels make more) \u2014 feeding them is a LAST RESORT: only when the\n  board is congested or nothing cheaper fits. Spawning cheap food from the\n  grave is usually better than sacrificing a generator. `get_board_state`\n  may show a `Best feed:` hint \u2014 the code's recommended feed target; follow\n  it when you agree. Keep at least one creature on the board for the merge\n  pipeline (don't strip it bare), and never feed stations or the\n  NecroMerger.\n  NEVER feed a merge-chain PRECURSOR of an ACTIVE craving: a precursor\n  is a same-family item whose level is BELOW the craving's level\n  (e.g. for a `Skeleton (lvl 3)` craving, `skeleton_lvl1`, `skeleton_lvl2`,\n  `ribcage`, and `bone` are all precursors \u2014 they merge up into the\n  craved monster, so feeding them destroys the path to fulfilling the\n  craving). Cells at the craving's exact level still feed normally\n  (they count toward the quota), and cells ABOVE the craving's level\n  still feed (they can't merge down). For a `Skeleton (lvl 1) 0/1`\n  craving, the precursors are `bone` and `ribcage` (which merge up\n  into the craved lvl 1) \u2014 protect those and feed the lvl 1 directly.\n  Merge precursors toward the craving instead of feeding them to the\n  Devourer.\n- SPAWN-FIRST ON SPARSE BOARDS: when the board has an empty cell AND a\n  spawn station (e.g. grave or chest) can spawn, generic feed-to-progress\n  is SUSPENDED \u2014 spawn a fresh cheap-chain item for free instead of\n  sacrificing one of only a few creatures that could merge. The `Best\n  spawn:` hint fires in this case. Real reasons to feed still apply:\n  congestion (few empty cells), an active craving, a `(max level)`\n  target, or a near-done feed feat.\n- MERGE-MATERIAL: `bone`, `ribcage`, and any mid-chain levelled creature\n  whose next level is known are MERGE MATERIAL \u2014 feeding one of these\n  removes a member of a future merge pair, so the `Best feed:` hint\n  avoids them when a non-material or craved target exists. (See\n  FEED-TO-PROGRESS above for the full feed-selection policy.)\n- The Devourer may have an active CRAVING (bubble above the board; Food bonus\n  granted ONCE when the quota is fulfilled). If a creature matching the\n  craving at the EXACT level is on the board, FEED it \u2014 unless a\n  nearly-done feat of another kind outranks it (see MOVE PRIORITY), or the\n  bar is so full the feed would overflow past tolerance (see CRAVING\n  OVERFLOW \u2014 spawn to rebuild it instead). NEVER feed a same-family\n  LOWER-level precursor (it merges up into the craved monster); cells AT\n  or ABOVE the craving's level feed normally. `get_board_state` shows\n  `Cravings: <item> (lvl <N>) <done>/<required>, reward +<food>`; when no\n  craving is shown, call `get_cravings` to read it. The craved item is\n  never a station and never the NecroMerger.\n- NEVER feed any station to the Devourer. The wiki's stations are:\n  Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, Foul Chicken, Slime Vat, Altar,\n  Dark Stores, Lectern, Fridge, Portal, Crashed Saucer, Telepad, Soul\n  Grinder, Prism, Unexpected Parcel, Meteor, Throne (plus post-prestige\n  additions) \u2014 this is the canonical list, referenced as \"the station\n  list\" elsewhere. The game itself permits feeding most stations behind a\n  confirmation dialog, but we never risk it. The NecroMerger is never fed,\n  spawned, or collected.\n  MERGING stations is normal and valid: two identical manapools, Graves,\n  etc. merge into the next level (e.g. manapool_lvl1 + manapool_lvl1 ->\n  manapool_lvl2) exactly like any other item pair. So the Mana Pool is\n  NOT a \"don't touch\" station: it merges like any item, and the grave's\n  popup even says \"Merge to level up\". Only the fixed NecroMerger is\n  never merged.\n- A Champion (e.g. The Peasant, The Knight, The Cleric, The Paladin,\n  The Rival, The Protector, The Mech, The King) may invade the board and\n  occupy a cell. It is an ENEMY, not a rune or a regular item: it can never\n  be merged, spawned, or fed as food. Champions are also NOT a target\n  themselves for `feed` or `merge` (the validators refuse). To damage a\n  Champion, drag a creature ONTO the Champion cell \u2014 that is the `attack`\n  action, a special move distinct from merge/spawn/feed. The Peasant is a\n  small human sprite \u2014 do NOT mistake it for a poison rune or any other\n  item. When `get_board_state` labels an item `(dmg N)`, that N is the\n  damage it deals if dropped on a Champion \u2014 so decide between feeding the\n  creature (its `(feed N)` food, capped by remaining satiety) and using it\n  to attack the Champion (its `(dmg N)`). Per observation, Champions do\n  not auto-attack you; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature\n  on the board has a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available;\n  merge/feed instead.\n- NEVER name an unidentified cell from the screenshot. If `get_board_state`\n  lists a cell as unidentified, call `identify_item` on it to learn what it\n  is \u2014 never guess a template id (like poisonrune_lvl1) from the pixels.\n  (Skip the call if a higher-priority move is available, e.g. a champion\n  is on the board or a feed-it-or-lose-it craving is nearly complete \u2014\n  unidentified cells can wait one step.)\n- MOVE PRIORITY (driven by ACTIVE FEATS): the `Feats (tier N):` line of\n  `get_board_state` lists every active task with its parsed action kind\n  (`[merge]` / `[feed]` / `[spawn]` / `[collect]`, or just the feat name\n  when the kind couldn't be parsed) and progress, flagging `NEAR DONE`\n  at >= 80% completion. Done feats are listed under `| done:` and no\n  longer steer. Spend each move advancing the objective closest to\n  completion: a task needing merges -> merge; feeds -> feed; spawns ->\n  spawn; collects -> collect. The current CRAVING is a feed objective\n  too (feeding the craved creature counts toward the quota; the Food\n  bonus is granted once the craving is fulfilled), and it usually\n  outweighs a merge unless a competing feat is closer to done. Combat\n  feats (e.g. `Beat The Peasant twice.`) and station-build feats (e.g.\n  `Build a Mana Pool.`) follow the same target kind: combat -> use\n  `attack` on a Champion; build -> use `buy_station`. The `Best merge:`\n  / `Best feed:` / `Best spawn:` / `Best attack:` / `Best income:`\n  hints on the board state follow the same weighting \u2014 they're HINTS,\n  not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better move. When\n  NO feat or craving steers the move, fall back to: merge two identical\n  items > feed (feed-to-progress; but when the board is sparse and a\n  grave can spawn, spawn instead \u2014 see SPAWN-FIRST) > spawn > collect\n  > idle. Skip `spawn` when the mana bar is low (it no-ops); skip\n  `collect` when the mana bar is full. `get_board_state` may also show\n  a `Champion:` line (next champion to spawn + progress); when a\n  champion is on the board, the attack branch becomes live.\n- The bottom of the lair screen has a dock of 5 buttons: Feats, Station,\n  Queue (placement action \u2014 tapping DROPS the queued reward onto the\n  board, so leave it alone unless you want the item placed), Spellbook\n  and Shop (both locked). `get_board_state` shows the live dock state in\n  a `Bottom bar:` line \u2014 trust that, not this static description.\n   A missing `Bottom bar:` line means a panel or non-lair screen is open,\n   so the dock is hidden.\n- POTIONS (manapot / manapotion): max-level Potions (e.g. `manapotion_lvl3`,\n  `manapot_lvl3`) are FEEDABLE consumables, NOT stations \u2014 they grant the\n  matching Resource (Mana) when fed, plus a small food value. The\n  in-game popup says \"Feed to the Devourer.\" with no merge line (they\n  are max-level, single-use). DO NOT confuse them with `manapool` (a\n  Resource-CAPACITY station that boosts Mana cap). The wiki's manapotion\n  lvl 3 grants 100% of Mana cap when fed \u2014 if the Mana bar is already\n  at 100% the feed is wasted (the Mana can't be stored). The validator\n  refuses `feed` on a manapot/manapotion when the Mana bar is at 100%\n  (`feed_mana_overflow`); feed potions only when you have Mana headroom,\n  or build a Mana Pool to raise the cap first.\n\nEach step you receive an automatic `get_board_state` result (the bot calls it\non your behalf every step) with the live board: occupied cells with their\ntemplate-bank ids, levels, and confidence scores; unidentified occupied cells\n(candidates for `identify_item`); the bottom bar state; the mana bar fill;\nthe current craving; the active strategy; and the feat list with action\nkinds + progress. The bot ALSO runs a PROACTIVE batch `identify_item` round\nup-front when there are UNID cells (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` per step) so\nyou can plan moves with full knowledge \u2014 check the tool-result message just\nabove the board state for what was identified. You can still call\n`identify_item` yourself in the optional-tools round for any cells the\nproactive round missed (capped at `MAX_DISCOVERY` cells per batch). The board state also shows one or more of these HINTS \u2014\nthe single highest-priority move under your current feats + craving:\n  - `Best merge: <id> (<r>,<c>)+(<r>,<c>) -> <result>` \u2014 top merge pair\n  - `Best feed: <id> (<r>,<c>) (feed N)` \u2014 top feed target\n  - `Best spawn: <station_id> (r,c) -> <item> (<X> empty)` \u2014 top spawn target. The hint points at the HIGHEST-LEVEL spawn station on the board. Per the wiki, grave_lvl1 spawns bone (100%), grave_lvl2 spawns bone (60%)/ribcage (40%), grave_lvl3 spawns bone (40%)/ribcage (30%)/zombie (30%). Chests outrank graves since chests are finite-use. The cell id includes the level (e.g. `grave_lvl3`) so you can see it at a glance, and the per-level rates are read from the glossary's popup block when available (per-level `lvl3 spawn: ...` line banked by the auto popup-reader).\n  - `Best attack: <creature> (r,c) (dmg N) -> champion (r,c)` \u2014 when a champion is on the board\n  - `Best income: <stack> (r,c) \u2014 feed it to the Devourer for <ICE/POISON/BLOOD/MOON/DEATH> RUNES / GOLD / GEMS (the income target of the active economy)` \u2014 fires when a max-level Rune, Coin, or Gem stack is on the board. Rune stacks fire under a build strategy (Runes are station-buying currency); Coin and Gem stacks fire unconditionally (more Gold/Gems is always useful for the Shop / skins / Wobulan trades). Sub-max income stacks are not valid `feed` targets \u2014 the validator refuses them, and the merge ranking merges them up first.\nThese are HINTS, not commands: follow them unless you see a clearly better\nmove, and prefer them over feed/spawn/collect/attack when one is listed.\nThe board state also shows `Feats (tier N): ...` listing every task with\nits `[kind]` and progress (`NEAR DONE` >= 80%), plus `Satiety: X/M\n(R remaining)` when the satiety fraction can be read \u2014 feed items only\nwhile R > 0 and only items whose `(feed N)` fits R.\nYou may also call `identify_item` on an unidentified cell to learn what it\nis \u2014 it opens the item's info popup, reads its description + merge-chain\ntext, and banks the sprite in the template bank (recorded in your item\nglossary). New items that appear from merges/spawns are popup-read\nautomatically, so `get_board_state` already flags max-level cells and\nlocks in the right id. Only call `identify_item` when a cell is\nUNIDENTIFIED (no template label) \u2014 never for cells that already show a\nlabel you don't recognize (the label is the truth; the sprite is the\nlie).\nAnd `get_cravings` reads the current craving \u2014 `get_board_state` already\nshows it from a recent read, so only call when none is shown or progress\nis stale. `tap_button` opens a dock panel (FEATS or STATION), read-only;\nthe feats are ALSO in `get_board_state`, so use it only for the full\npanel or fresh progress.\nAnd `set_strategy` is YOUR strategic voice: commit to ONE active feat OR a meta-goal,\nand the priority layer boosts YOUR choice for ~15 steps instead of the\nclosest-to-done default. When feats compete or you see a better long-\nterm play than the default ordering, CALL IT (consider it at least once\nafter each Feats refresh \u2014 the Feats line on the board state is the\nsignal that a refresh happened). Your active strategy shows in\n`get_board_state`.\n\nSTRATEGY TYPES:\n  - EXPLICIT FEAT (takes priority over meta-goals):\n    - STATION feat (`Build a X.` or `Own a Lvl N+ X.` where X is a station\n      like Grave, Mana Pool, Supply Cupboard, etc.): the feat needs the X\n      STATION bought from the Station panel. DO NOT set `target_item` \u2014\n      the station isn't on the board to merge toward; `buy_station` is the\n      action. The X station costs Runes (Mana Pool = ice + poison, Slime\n      Vat = poison + blood, Dark Stores = blood + moon, etc. \u2014 check the\n      `cost_cache` or call `buy_station(family, confirm=false)` to see the\n      current prices; feed max-level Rune stacks for the income boost).\n    - CREATURE feat (`Own a Lvl N+ Y.` where Y is a creature like Skeleton,\n      Zombie, Eye Monster, Spider, Mummy, Bat, Shade, Abomination, etc.,\n      or a champion like Peasant, Knight, Gorgon, Cyclops, Harpy): the\n      feat needs the creature merged/collected on the board. Set\n      `target_item` to the creature's family + level (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`\n      for an `Own a Lvl 3+ Skeleton.` feat). A `target_item` whose family\n      doesn't match the feat's noun is dropped silently \u2014 the bot only\n      trusts a target that's the right shape.\n    - OTHER feat (combat, action count, collect-Nx, level-N, etc., e.g.\n      `Beat The Peasant twice.`, `Merge things 50 times.`, `Reach Devourer\n      level 5.`): no station or creature direction. `target_item` is\n      ignored. The priority layer does not boost a station/creature kind\n      for these \u2014 the action is whatever the feat text describes.\n\n  - META-GOAL (used when no explicit feat applies, or to override):\n    Set `meta_goal` to ONE of:\n      - slime_generation: slime is low \u2192 prioritize slimevat builds, slime-producing minions\n      - mana_generation: mana is low \u2192 prioritize manapool builds, mana-producing minions\n      - rune_economy: rune balances low \u2192 prioritize chest spawns, rune merges, rune feeds\n      - champion_combat: champion present \u2192 prioritize high-damage minions, attack\n      - board_management: board congested \u2192 merge aggressively, feed non-critical\n      - feeding_optimization: satiety near cap \u2192 feed efficiently, avoid overflow\n      - darkness_generation: darkness low \u2192 prioritize darkstores builds\n    When using a meta-goal, set `target_family` to the family to build toward\n    (e.g. \"manapool\" for mana_generation, \"slimevat\" for slime_generation,\n    \"grave\" for rune_economy, \"darkstores\" for darkness_generation).\n    Explicit feats ALWAYS take priority over meta-goals.\n\nThe `target_family` field replaces `target_item` for station/meta-goal strategies.\nFor creature feats, you may still use `target_item` (e.g. `skeleton_lvl3`).\nAnd `buy_station` spends RUNES (ice, poison, blood, moon, death) to place\na NEW station. Two-phase (ENFORCED): confirm=false reads the dialog and\nstashes a pending buy; the next call MUST be confirm=true (same family)\nor it auto-expires. Only confirm purchases serving your strategy\n(`strategy_mismatch` refuses other families). GATHER Runes by feeding\nmax-level Rune stacks (see ICE CHEST above; the `Best income:` hint fires\nunder a build strategy). Full semantics are in the tool description \u2014\nthis is the summary.\nAnd `collect_queue` places the dock Queue button's reward onto the board\n(bare skull = empty); REFUSED when congested. Board chests are different:\nthey are spawn stations \u2014 tap with `spawn` (see ICE CHEST). Full\nsemantics are in the tool description.\n\nHARD RULES (every violation is rejected \u2014 do not test them):\n1. Merge ONLY two cells with the SAME id; NEVER merge [NEVER MERGE] / (max level) cells.\n2. Spawn ONLY on [SPAWNABLE] cells (grave needs Mana + room; chest needs room; cupboard needs Slime + room and an eye objective) \u2014 never on runes, creatures, or full boards.\n3. Feed ONLY [FEEDABLE] cells; never feed stations, champions, or the NecroMerger.\n4. Attack ONLY as your creature (with dmg N) -> champion cell; a champion is NEVER the attacker.\n5. get_board_state / identify_item / buy_station / set_strategy are TOOLS, not actions \u2014 never output them.\n\nExample legal move: {\"action\": \"feed\", \"cell\": [1,0]} where (1,0) is tagged [FEEDABLE].\nExample illegal move (always rejected, do not repeat this shape): {\"action\": \"merge\", \"a\": [1,0], \"b\": [3,2]} where both cells are tagged [NEVER MERGE] \u2014 the validator refuses merge_max_level and the game no-ops.\n\nThen look at the screenshot, decide the single best move, and reply with ONLY a\nJSON object using EXACTLY one of these actions:\n{\"action\":\"merge\",\"a\":[r,c],\"b\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"spawn\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"feed\",\"cell\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"attack\",\"cell\":[r,c],\"target\":[r,c]}\n{\"action\":\"collect\"}\n{\"action\":\"idle\"}\nr is the row (0-4), c is the column (0-3). merge: pick two\ncells holding the SAME item (identical sprites, same id, same level). spawn: on\na spawn station (grave \u2014 costs Mana; or chest \u2014 mana-free, one Rune per\ntap; the chest on the board is a `spawn` cell, not a `collect` cell).\nattack: drag one of YOUR creatures (a non-champion, non-station cell with a\nknown `(dmg N)` value) onto a Champion cell (a cell labeled `(champion)` in\nget_board_state \u2014 e.g. The Peasant) to deal that creature's `(dmg N)` HP to\nthe Champion. The `cell` (attacker) is ALWAYS one of YOUR creatures \u2014 a\nChampion can NEVER be the attacker (the validator refuses `attack_is_champion`),\nonly the `target` is the Champion. Per observation, Champions do not\nauto-attack; only your attack drags deal damage. If no creature on the board\nhas a known `(dmg N)` value, attack is not available; merge/feed instead.\ncollect: tap the NecroMerger at (0,3) to gain Mana. It does NOT\nremove the NecroMerger, does NOT clear or free a board cell, and you cannot\n\"collect\" any other item \u2014 chests and stations (Grave, Mana Pool, etc.)\nand creatures are never \"collected\" (use `spawn` for a chest, `feed`\nfor a creature, `buy_station` for a station).\nfeed: drag a creature into the Devourer's mouth. Never feed any station\n(the station list above) and never the NecroMerger.\nDo not explain, just output the JSON object.\nAnd `lookup_wiki` fetches a NecroMerger wiki page to fact-check item behavior or merge chains you are unsure about \u2014 prefer what the board and popups tell you, and only use it when genuinely uncertain.\n\nPast learnings (apply them if relevant):\nCommitted fact learnings (apply these):\n- [fact] Grave_lvl3 spawns bone, ribcage, or zombie with 100% probability when tapped.\n- [fact] Grave_lvl1 spawns bone when tapped.\n\nTentative fact learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [fact] Never feed a Champion to the Devourer. A Champion is defeated by dragging a creature onto it, not by feeding.\n\nCommitted pattern learnings (apply these):\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl1 grants +10 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl2 grants +60 Feed.\n- [pattern] Feeding a Skeleton_lvl4 grants +140 Feed.\n- [pattern] Bone items can be merged together to form Rib Cages.\n- [pattern] Two Bone items merge to produce a Rib Cage with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Two Skeleton_lvl2 items can be merged to produce a Skeleton_lvl3.\n- [pattern] Rib Cages can be merged to summon Skeletons with +2 Feed.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl1 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl0 items (though not visible in this window).\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 spawns bone or ribcage with 60% and 40% probability respectively.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl7 spawns from merging two Skeleton_lvl6 items.\n- [pattern] Skeleton_lvl7 is the highest level visible and grants +1500 Feed when fed.\n- [pattern] Grave_lvl2 is the highest level visible and can spawn bone or ribcage.\n- [pattern] Merging two Skeleton_lvl3 items summons a Skeleton_lvl4.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl5 is the highest level visible in this window and can be merged to produce a higher level.\n- [pattern] A Skeleton_lvl3 can be summoned by merging two Skeleton_lvl2 items.\n\nTentative anti-pattern learnings (treat as tentative):\n- [anti-pattern] Don't feed a mid-chain merge component (bone, ribcage, or an item that can still merge up) while a non-mergeable feedable exists \u2014 merge-material exists to build merges, feeding it destroys pairs.\n- [anti-pattern] Never feed a Station to the Devourer \u2014 stations are board fixtures, not food.\n\nItems you have learned to recognize (apply if relevant):\n## Item coins_lvl2 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 5\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeball (popup)\n\n- feed value: 15\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye in a Jar.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie_lvl5 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 1000\n- damage value: 300\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Zombie.\n- edge: zombie -> zombie\n  [source: popup]\n## Item eyeinajar (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item cauldron (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn potions.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item necromancer (popup)\n\n- feed value: 60\n- damage value: 25\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item ribcage (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to summon a Skeleton.\n- edge: two Rib Cage -> Skeleton\n- edge: ribcage -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl6 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 300\n- damage value: 100\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton_lvl4 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 140\n- damage value: 50\n- description: Merge to summon a higher lvl Skeleton.\n- edge: two Skeleton -> Skeleton of the next level\n- edge: skeleton -> skeleton\n  [source: popup]\n## Item valuablechest (spawn)\n\n- spawn: valuablechest -> coins_lvl1, coins_lvl2, gems_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl1 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl2 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl3 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl4 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl4 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item fridge_lvl5 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: fridge_lvl5 -> eyeinjar\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item valuablechest (popup)\n\n- description: Tap to spawn items.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item icerunes_lvl1 (popup)\n\n- feed value: 2\n- description: Merge to create a bigger pile or feed to the Devourer.\n  [source: popup]\n## Item skeleton (chain)\n\n- merge chain: bone -> ribcage -> skeleton_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icerune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: icerune_lvl1 -> icerune_lvl2 -> icerune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item poisonrune (chain)\n\n- merge chain: poisonrune_lvl1 -> poisonrune_lvl2 -> poisonrune_lvl3\n  [source: popup]\n## Item zombie (chain)\n\n- merge chain: rottenflesh -> severedhand -> zombie_lvl1\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item coins (chain)\n\n- merge chain: coins_lvl1 -> coins_lvl2 -> coins_lvl3 -> coins_lvl4\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item icebox_unopened (spawn)\n\n- spawn: icebox_unopened -> icerune_lvl1, icerune_lvl2, poisonrune_lvl1\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl1 -> bone\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl2 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl2 -> bone, ribcage\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: popup]\n## Item grave_lvl3 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: grave_lvl3 -> bone, ribcage, zombie\n- uses: 5\n  [source: popup]\n## Item supplycupboard_lvl1 (spawn)\n\n- spawn: supplycupboard_lvl1 -> eyeball\n- uses: infinite\n  [source: wiki]\n## Item sup