s and the current situation.\n\nFirst, looking at the occupied cells. There are several items here. The key points from the board state:\n\n- Empty cells: (1,0), (3,0), (3,1), (4,0), (4,1) \u2014 5 empty spots.\n- Best merge hint is eyeball (2,3) + (3,3). Both are labeled as [FEEDABLE] with scores 1.00 and 0.94. The merge would produce an Eye Monster, which is the current craving (since the craving bubble says \"eyemonster\").\n\nWait, the craving is for an Eye Monster. The user's board state shows a craving of eyemonster. So merging two eyeballs would create an Eye Monster. But the current cells have two eyeballs: one at (2,3) and another at (3,3). Wait, no\u2014the list says:\n\n- (2,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 1.00, margin 0.57)\n- (3,3) eyeball (feed 15) [FEEDABLE] (score 0.94, margin 0.53)\n\nSo there are two eyeballs on the board. The Best merge hint is to merge those two. But wait, the merge chain for eyeball: according to the item glossary, supplycupboard_lvl1 spawns eyeball, and then merging two eyeballs would make an Eye Monster (eyeinajar). Wait, no\u2014the popup says \"Merge to summon a Eye Monster.\" So yes, two eyeballs merge into an Eye Monster.\n\nBut the current craving is for an Eye Monster. So if we merge them, that would fulfill the craving. However, the Feats line shows \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" as a feat, but it's not completed yet (0/0). But the user might be trying to get the craving done.\n\nWait, the board state says \"Cravings (bubble): eyemonster\". So the current craving is for an Eye Monster. The Best merge hint is merging two eyeballs to make one Eye Monster. That would fulfill the craving. However, the Feats line mentions \"Own a lvl 5 Eye Monster\" but it's"}
